  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside and the High-affinity choline transporter, mediated through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence scores, with Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside acting as a target for the 26S proteasome subunit, which in turn targets the choline transporter. Two distinct compounds, 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and Nortoxiferine, also interact with the 26S proteasome subunit and ultimately with the choline transporter. The shared involvement of the 26S proteasome subunit indicates a possible mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may influence the choline transporter, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a plausible biological link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
